{%- comment -%}
  Is `uri` an acceptable redirect URI to REGISTER (OAuth 2.1 §2.3.1, RFC 8252 §7)?
    - https://… (any host), or
    - http:// on a loopback host (127.0.0.1, [::1], localhost) — native/CLI clients, or
    - a private-use scheme for native apps (e.g. vscode://, cursor://) — never the
      script-capable/local schemes javascript:, data:, vbscript:, file:, blob:.
  No fragment, no userinfo.

  @param {string} uri
  @return {boolean}
{%- endcomment -%}
{% liquid
  function u = 'modules/mcp/commands/oauth/parse_url', url: uri
  unless u.valid
    return false
  endunless
  if u.has_fragment or u.has_userinfo
    return false
  endif
  case u.scheme
    when 'https'
      return true
    when 'http'
      return u.is_loopback
    when 'javascript', 'data', 'vbscript', 'file', 'blob', 'about', 'ws', 'wss', 'ftp'
      return false
  endcase
  return true
%}
